& [PositiveAssertions] are mandatory
  + AcquisitionIdentity: Serialize plus DeserializeOwned
  + AcquisitionScopeClaim: Serialize plus DeserializeOwned
  + CompletionDisposition: Serialize plus DeserializeOwned
  + AcquisitionLineageMetadataClaim: Serialize plus DeserializeOwned
  + CausalOrderClaim: Serialize plus DeserializeOwned
  + OrderedAcquisitionPairMetadataClaim: Serialize plus DeserializeOwned
  + RepeatedInventoryEvidencePlan: Serialize plus DeserializeOwned

& [NegativeAssertions] are mandatory
  + WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest does not implement DeserializeOwned
  + AcquisitionLineageBinding does not implement DeserializeOwned
  + OrderedAcquisitionPairBinding does not implement DeserializeOwned
  + WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliation does not implement DeserializeOwned
  + RepeatedInventoryEvidenceClaim does not implement DeserializeOwned

& [ProofMechanism] uses stable compile-time ambiguity
  + a local assertion macro uses overlapping impl selection so compilation succeeds only when the tested type does not implement the forbidden trait
  + positive assertions use ordinary generic trait bounds
  + assertions live under cfg(test) in the one candidate module
  + no static_assertions or other dependency is added

& [PredecessorFacts] are exact
  + current digest carrier derives Clone Debug PartialEq Eq Serialize only
  + current reconciliation scope disposition and result derive Serialize only where carrier-bearing or output-only
  + carrier fields are private and current modules expose immutable getters only
  + no current carrier module change is necessary or permitted

& [SignatureStopConditions] are exact
  + any positive assertion fails
  + any negative assertion fails
  + any planned type requires a changed predecessor derive visibility field or constructor
  + any assertion requires a new dependency nightly feature unsafe or runtime approximation
  + any carrier-bearing value becomes accepted input transport

& [DesignDecision] is ready for executable proof only after the planned type skeleton exists under an implementation signature
  + canonical must bind these assertions as nonnegotiable acceptance criteria
  + phase lock may rely on Rust coherence analysis plus exact predecessor source hashes
  + final proof requires actual debug and release compilation of the assertions
  + implementation authority is absent
  + execution authority is absent
  + physical authority is absent
  + next is support-package and canonical generation with trait gate locked
